 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 508259,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Choose the correct inequality for the graph shown.\n<br>\n\n<img src=\"exercises/media/316a0299412331b8.png\" alt=\"A line is plotted on a coordinate plane. The horizontal and vertical axes range from negative 10 to 10, in increments of 5. The line passes through the points, (0, 5) and (4, negative 3). The region to the left of the line is shaded.\">\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 995756,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"y = -2x + 5\">y = -2x + 5</span>",
     "correctness": "0.0"
    },
    {
     "id": 995757,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"y \\leq -2x + 5\">y \\leq -2x + 5</span>",
     "correctness": "1.0"
    },
    {
     "id": 995758,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"y \\geq -2x + 5\">y \\geq -2x + 5</span>",
     "correctness": "0.0"
    },
    {
     "id": 995759,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"y < -2x + 5\">y &lt; -2x + 5</span>",
     "correctness": "0.0"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response",
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Test the points on the line and test points in the shaded are for all the options. Only the correct option works.</p>\n<p>Correct option: <span data-math=\"y \\le  - 2x + 5\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"(0, 5)\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"5 \\le  - 2\\left( 0 \\right) + 5\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"5 \\le 5\"></span> is true, so this ordered pair is a solution to the inequality and a point on the boundary.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"(4, -3)\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\" - 3 \\le  - 2\\left( 4 \\right) + 5\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\" - 3 \\le  - 8 + 5\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\" - 3 \\le  - 3\"></span> is true, so this ordered pair is a solution to the inequality and a point on the boundary.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"(0, 0)\"></span> to test shaded area.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0 \\le  - 2\\left( 0 \\right) + 5\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0 \\le 5\"></span> is true, so shade the side of the boundary where <span data-math=\"(0, 0)\"></span> is.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"y \\leq -2x + 5\">y \\leq -2x + 5</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
